@Chapter Introduction

The <Package>FusionSystems</Package> package tests whether saturated fusion
systems with given properties could exist on a finite <M>p</M>-group
<M>S</M>, without constructing them. Its main functions are:

* <Ref Attr="AllProtoEssentials" Label="for IsPGroup"/> finds the subgroups
  of <M>S</M> that could be essential in a saturated fusion system on
  <M>S</M>, up to <M>S</M>-conjugacy, and
  <Ref Oper="IsProtoEssential" Label="for IsPGroup, IsPGroup"/> tests a
  single subgroup (Chapters <Ref Chap="Chapter_ProtoEssentialSubgroups"/>
  and <Ref Chap="Chapter_ProtoEssentialChecks"/>);
* <Ref Attr="PossiblySupportsReducedFusionSystems" Label="for IsPGroup"/>
  tests whether <M>S</M> could support a reduced fusion system (Chapter
  <Ref Chap="Chapter_Checks_for_reduced_fusion_systems"/>);
* <Ref Oper="FindReducedSequences" Label="for IsPGroup, IsList"/> finds the
  automizer sequences that could lead to reduced fusion systems (Chapter
  <Ref Chap="Chapter_AutomizerSequences"/>).

The tests check necessary conditions only: a subgroup found to be
proto-essential, or a group that passes the tests for reduced fusion systems,
need not lead to an actual saturated fusion system.

To follow the progress of a longer computation, set the info level of
<C>InfoFusion</C> to 1 or higher.

@BeginExampleSession
gap> S := SmallGroup(2^7, 931);;
gap> Length(AllProtoEssentials(S));
5
gap> PossiblySupportsReducedFusionSystems(S);
true
@EndExampleSession
